From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: denny <dennis.sheirer@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:11:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Read a register before control writes that can follow an idle
 gap

While the device is streaming, the RTL2832U stalls the first vendor OUT
control transfer that follows roughly 100-300 ms without control
traffic, and libusb reports LIBUSB_ERROR_PIPE (-9). Back-to-back
transfers succeed. It shows as "rtlsdr_demod_write_reg failed with -9"
when a streaming device is retuned, and the I2C repeater write that
fails can take the tuner write after it with it. rtlsdr_read_eeprom
fails with -3 every time while streaming.

A vendor IN transfer just before the write prevents the stall. Read a
demod register, the same one rtlsdr_demod_write_reg already reads after
each write, before writes in rtlsdr_demod_write_reg and
rtlsdr_write_reg, and at the start of the EEPROM functions.

rtlsdr_write_array, which carries the tuner's I2C traffic, does not
read first. Tuner access always starts with the I2C repeater write, and
reading before every I2C write doubles the tuning time.

Measured on an R820T dongle streaming at 2.4 MS/s. Lines reporting -9
over 12 operations one second apart, and the mean time of each call
made back to back:

                   retune  gain  sample rate   set_center_freq  set_tuner_gain
  unpatched          13     13       25            91 ms            38 ms
  patched             0      0        0            96 ms            43 ms
  read before every
  write, for scale    0      0        0           186 ms            73 ms

rtlsdr_read_eeprom while streaming: -3 every time unpatched, succeeds
patched.
---
 src/librtlsdr.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/librtlsdr.c b/src/librtlsdr.c
index 82bab6d..6d73514 100644
--- a/src/librtlsdr.c
+++ b/src/librtlsdr.c
@@ -405,6 +405,25 @@ enum blocks {
 	IICB			= 6,
 };
 
+/*
+ * While the device is streaming, the RTL2832U stalls (LIBUSB_ERROR_PIPE) the
+ * first vendor OUT control transfer that follows roughly 100-300 ms without
+ * control traffic. A vendor IN transfer just before it prevents the stall, so
+ * the write paths that can follow an idle gap read a demod register first: the
+ * same register that rtlsdr_demod_write_reg already reads after each write.
+ *
+ * rtlsdr_write_array, which carries the tuner's I2C traffic, does not read
+ * first: tuner access always starts with the I2C repeater write, which is a
+ * demod write, and doubling the transfers would double the tuning time.
+ */
+static void rtlsdr_ctrl_wake(rtlsdr_dev_t *dev)
+{
+	unsigned char data;
+
+	libusb_control_transfer(dev->devh, CTRL_IN, 0, (0x01 << 8) | 0x20, 0x0a,
+				&data, 1, CTRL_TIMEOUT);
+}
+
 int rtlsdr_read_array(rtlsdr_dev_t *dev, uint8_t block, uint16_t addr, uint8_t *array, uint8_t len)
 {
 	int r;
@@ -503,6 +522,7 @@ int rtlsdr_write_reg(rtlsdr_dev_t *dev, uint8_t block, uint16_t addr, uint16_t v
 
 	data[1] = val & 0xff;
 
+	rtlsdr_ctrl_wake(dev);
 	r = libusb_control_transfer(dev->devh, CTRL_OUT, 0, addr, index, data, len, CTRL_TIMEOUT);
 
 	if (r < 0)
@@ -544,6 +564,7 @@ int rtlsdr_demod_write_reg(rtlsdr_dev_t *dev, uint8_t page, uint16_t addr, uint1
 
 	data[1] = val & 0xff;
 
+	rtlsdr_ctrl_wake(dev);
 	r = libusb_control_transfer(dev->devh, CTRL_OUT, 0, addr, index, data, len, CTRL_TIMEOUT);
 
 	if (r < 0)
@@ -833,6 +854,7 @@ int rtlsdr_write_eeprom(rtlsdr_dev_t *dev, uint8_t *data, uint8_t offset, uint16
 	if ((len + offset) > 256)
 		return -2;
 
+	rtlsdr_ctrl_wake(dev);
 	for (i = 0; i < len; i++) {
 		cmd[0] = i + offset;
 		r = rtlsdr_write_array(dev, IICB, EEPROM_ADDR, cmd, 1);
@@ -870,6 +892,7 @@ int rtlsdr_read_eeprom(rtlsdr_dev_t *dev, uint8_t *data, uint8_t offset, uint16_
 	if ((len + offset) > 256)
 		return -2;
 
+	rtlsdr_ctrl_wake(dev);
 	r = rtlsdr_write_array(dev, IICB, EEPROM_ADDR, &offset, 1);
 	if (r < 0)
 		return -3;
